IMPORT prelude

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore) -- when the Act applies to a contract (s 1), when a person who is not a
-- party may enforce a term (s 2) and the contracts where s 2 confers no right (s 7), when the parties need that person's consent to
-- rescind or vary (s 3) and when a court may dispense with it, the reduction for what the promisee has already recovered (s 6), and
-- the third party's place in an arbitration agreement (s 9(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CRTPA2001.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendments annotated in
-- the body are [40/2019] (s 3(7)) and [5/2021] (s 7(6), (7)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: it decides whether someone named in another
-- person's contract -- a family member on a travel or insurance booking, a buyer of goods delivered to someone else, a subcontractor
-- shielded by an exclusion clause -- can sue on it. The Act is short (nine sections), so nearly all of it is encoded. Not encoded:
-- the defences, set-off and counterclaim available to the promisor (s 4) beyond a note, the promisee's own rights (s 5, a saving
-- only), the savings and cross-references in s 8 (other rights, Unfair Contract Terms Act, Limitation Act, other written law), the
-- Minister's orders naming rail and road conventions (s 7(6)(b), (c)), and s 9(2).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001`

§§ `1 -- contracts the Act applies to`

-- s 1(2): "this Act does not apply in relation to a contract entered into before the end of the period of 6 months from
-- 1 January 2002." (3): that restriction does not apply to a contract which "(a) is entered into on or after 1 January 2002; and
-- (b) expressly provides for the application of this Act."
-- Dates are written as YYYYMMDD numbers. INFERENCE: the 6-month period is read as ending at the close of 30 June 2002, so a
-- contract made on or after 1 July 2002 is covered. The text does not give the end date.
GIVEN `date entered` IS A NUMBER, `expressly provides for the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the contract` IF
        `date entered` AT LEAST 20020701
    OR  (`date entered` AT LEAST 20020101 AND `expressly provides for the Act`)

§§ `2 and 7 -- who may enforce a term`

-- s 7: s 2 "does not confer any right on a third party" for (1) a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument;
-- (2) a contract binding on a company and its members under s 39 of the Companies Act 1967; (3) an LLP registration document or LLP
-- agreement; (4) "to enforce any term of a contract of employment against an employee"; (5) a contract for the carriage of goods by
-- sea, or by rail or road, or of cargo by air, subject to an international transport convention -- "except that a third party may
-- in reliance on that section avail the third party of an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract."
DECLARE `Kind of contract` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary contract`
    `a negotiable instrument`
    `a company constitution`
    `an LLP agreement or registration document`
    `an employment contract enforced against the employee`
    `an employment contract enforced against the employer`
    `a contract for carriage of goods by sea`
    `a convention contract for carriage by air, rail or road`

-- s 2(1): a third party "may, in the third party's own right, enforce a term of the contract if -- (a) the contract expressly
-- provides that the third party may; or (b) subject to subsection (2), the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party."
-- (2): (1)(b) does not apply "if, on a proper construction of the contract, it appears that the parties did not intend the term to
-- be enforceable by the third party." (3): the third party "must be expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a
-- class or as answering a particular description, but need not be in existence when the contract is entered into."
-- (6): where a term excludes or limits liability, "enforcing" the term means availing oneself of the exclusion or limitation.
-- The non-intention in (2) defeats only limb (b); an express provision under limb (a) survives it.
DECLARE Term HAS
    `the contract is of kind` IS A `Kind of contract`
    `the contract expressly says the third party may enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term purports to benefit the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties did not intend third-party enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the third party is expressly identified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term excludes or limits liability` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the term` IS A Term
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 is excluded by section 7` IF
    CONSIDER `the term`'s `the contract is of kind`
    WHEN `an ordinary contract` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an employment contract enforced against the employer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contract for carriage of goods by sea` THEN NOT `the term`'s `the term excludes or limits liability`
    WHEN `a convention contract for carriage by air, rail or road` THEN NOT `the term`'s `the term excludes or limits liability`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the term` IS A Term
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limb of section 2(1) is met` IF
        `the term`'s `the contract expressly says the third party may enforce`
    OR  (`the term`'s `the term purports to benefit the third party`
         AND (NOT `the term`'s `the parties did not intend third-party enforcement`))

GIVEN `the term` IS A Term
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the third party may enforce the term` IF
        `a limb of section 2(1) is met` `the term`
    AND `the term`'s `the third party is expressly identified`
    AND (NOT `section 2 is excluded by section 7` `the term`)

§§ `3(1) to (3) -- when the third party's consent is needed to rescind or vary`

-- s 3(1): the parties "may not, by agreement, rescind the contract, or vary the contract in such a way as to extinguish or alter the
-- third party's entitlement under that right, without the third party's consent if -- (a) the third party has communicated the third
-- party's assent to the term to the promisor; (b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term ...; or (c) the
-- promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact
-- relied on the term".
-- (2): assent "may be by words or conduct" and, if sent by post or other means, "is not to be regarded as communicated to the
-- promisor until the assent is received by the promisor."
-- (3): (1) is subject to an express term that (a) lets the parties rescind or vary without consent, or (b) requires consent "in
-- circumstances specified in the contract instead of" those in (1)(a), (b) and (c).
-- A posted assent that has not arrived does not lock the contract, whatever the third party believes.
DECLARE `Variation facts` HAS
    `the third party has a section 2 right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the third party sent assent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the promisor received the assent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the promisor knows of reliance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reliance was foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the third party in fact relied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an express term allows variation without consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an express term substitutes its own circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract's own circumstances hold` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `v` IS A `Variation facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `assent has been communicated` IF
    `v`'s `the third party sent assent` AND `v`'s `the promisor received the assent`

GIVEN `v` IS A `Variation facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 3(1) ground exists` IF
        `assent has been communicated` `v`
    OR  `v`'s `the promisor knows of reliance`
    OR  (`v`'s `reliance was foreseeable` AND `v`'s `the third party in fact relied`)

GIVEN `v` IS A `Variation facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the third party's consent is needed to rescind or vary` IF
        `v`'s `the third party has a section 2 right`
    AND (NOT `v`'s `an express term allows variation without consent`)
    AND (    (`v`'s `an express term substitutes its own circumstances` AND `v`'s `the contract's own circumstances hold`)
         OR  ((NOT `v`'s `an express term substitutes its own circumstances`) AND `a section 3(1) ground exists` `v`))

§§ `3(4) to (7) -- dispensing with consent`

-- s 3(4): on the parties' application the court or arbitral tribunal "may" dispense with consent required under (1) or (3) if
-- "(a) the consent cannot be obtained because the third party's whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained; or (b) the third
-- party is mentally incapable of giving the third party's consent." (5): it may also dispense with consent required "under
-- subsection (1)(c)" if "it cannot reasonably be ascertained whether or not the third party has in fact relied on the term".
-- (6): it may impose conditions, "including a condition requiring the payment of compensation to the third party".
-- (7): the court's power is exercisable by "both the General Division of the High Court and a District Court".
-- This returns whether the power is AVAILABLE; whether to exercise it is the court's discretion and is not modelled.
-- The uncertain-reliance ground is tied to (1)(c); it is not available where consent is required on the assent or awareness
-- grounds, or on the contract's own substituted circumstances.
DECLARE `Consent ground` IS ONE OF
    `assent communicated`
    `promisor aware of reliance`
    `foreseeable reliance`
    `circumstances specified in the contract`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Consent ground`, `whereabouts unknown` IS A BOOLEAN, `mentally incapable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reliance cannot be ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may dispense with consent` IF
        `whereabouts unknown`
    OR  `mentally incapable`
    OR  (`reliance cannot be ascertained` AND
            CONSIDER `the ground`
            WHEN `foreseeable reliance` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE)

GIVEN `the court` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court has the dispensing power` IF
        `the court` EQUALS "General Division of the High Court"
    OR  `the court` EQUALS "District Court"

§§ `6 -- no double liability`

-- s 6: where the promisee "has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of -- (a) the third party's loss in respect of the term;
-- or (b) the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor", the court or tribunal "must
-- reduce any award to the third party to such extent as it thinks appropriate to take account of the sum recovered".
-- The DUTY to reduce is mandatory; the AMOUNT is discretionary, so only the duty is encoded. A sum the promisee recovered for its
-- own loss does not trigger s 6.
DECLARE `What the promisee recovered for` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `the third party's loss`
    `the cost of making good the default to the third party`
    `the promisee's own loss`

GIVEN `recovery` IS A `What the promisee recovered for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the award to the third party must be reduced` IF
    CONSIDER `recovery`
    WHEN `the third party's loss` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the cost of making good the default to the third party` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `9(1) -- arbitration`

-- s 9(1): where "(a) a right under section 2 to enforce a term ... is subject to a term providing for the submission of disputes to
-- arbitration ...; and (b) the arbitration agreement is an agreement in writing for the purposes of the Arbitration Act 2001 or
-- Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994, the third party is treated ... as a party to the arbitration agreement as
-- regards disputes between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term".
-- s 4 (NOT ENCODED BEYOND THIS NOTE): the promisor keeps defences and set-off it would have had against the promisee, and those it
-- would have had against the third party as if a party; s 4(6) stops a third party relying on a term it could not have relied on as
-- a party.
GIVEN `right is subject to an arbitration term` IS A BOOLEAN, `arbitration agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `dispute is with the promisor about enforcing the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` IF
    `right is subject to an arbitration term` AND `arbitration agreement is in writing` AND `dispute is with the promisor about enforcing the term`
